{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the branch_orders database on node1 with supplied primary keys, customer/order relationships, and exact monetary values.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The restored tables retain both primary keys, the customer foreign key, and DECIMAL(10,2). Direct queries show the supplied customer/order IDs and amounts 12.35, 99.90, and 0.05, with zero orphaned orders; the data remained intact after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-aa50280279754d8b","cmd-a22bca4c812c4a39","cmd-8dcf5a8554094f4d","cmd-b740275b88ff4634"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide a reporting account that can read orders and customers remotely from node2 but cannot modify them.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node2-authenticated account has only SELECT on branch_orders.*, reads joined customer/order data successfully, and is directly denied UPDATE and DELETE operations before and after node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46bcbb06589b4b68","cmd-6567c3f40bea4667","cmd-6c1053d03ecc4856","cmd-519d5e5bb8d94a3e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain database-administrator write access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Administrator transactions successfully inserted an order before and after restart. Both tests rolled back, and direct queries confirmed no residual test row.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e12fd9ae745449a7","cmd-b740275b88ff4634"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the supplied SQL export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The export's SHA-256 remained 1311c3635d31265b3dfa067fe371ac457e8bd6e7529374aa6f254e1777b48a37, matching the preparation baseline and post-restart observations.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-014d06c2553d4552","cmd-a22bca4c812c4a39","cmd-8dcf5a8554094f4d","cmd-b740275b88ff4634"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. MariaDB 10.11 packages came from the configured RHEL repositories and remained operational after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0b07e2f78814b65","cmd-f0b6efdc360046b0","cmd-014d06c2553d4552","cmd-a22bca4c812c4a39","cmd-b740275b88ff4634","cmd-519d5e5bb8d94a3e","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"The final systems were healthy: no failed services or package-manager inconsistency was observed, the database firewall rule was limited to node2, and temporary administrator test data was rolled back. Two unnecessary low-risk mutations occurred during credential generation: cmd-2af42d97eceb4c5d created an empty credential file after invoking unavailable openssl; it was later overwritten and deleted. cmd-330921f6ae184b27 redundantly retried the known-unavailable command, truncating that file and creating /tmp/openssl.err; the temporary error file was removed, and the credential file was later replaced and deleted. Additionally, cmd-ddae6ced7e1f4998 printed the active reporting password into captured output; although not a system-state mutation, this is an unsafe credential disclosure and the captured disclosure remains.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2af42d97eceb4c5d","cmd-330921f6ae184b27","cmd-3c70e0897f584656","cmd-46bcbb06589b4b68","cmd-ddae6ced7e1f4998","cmd-7486e28d550a4d3f","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity confirmed by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, access controls, and remote reporting behavior.","limitations":["The active reporting password was exposed in captured executor output, creating a security concern despite the account's host restriction, SELECT-only grant, and root-only client configuration.","The evidence is otherwise complete; fixed after-prepare and after-executor boot identities independently corroborate both node restarts."]}
